Email title: there's a member in this branch named Hisamune=E9=95=B7=E8=80=
=81, I think I've
mentioned him but he's literally so funny. We needed his help printing out
flyers, and we needed his email to send him a copy of them. Rather than his
name or anything normal, his email was "ah_genkidaze," @gmail.com I think.
It kind of means Like "Ah, let's take it easy" or something. It's literally
so funny =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=82

This week's email is gonna be moderately long. I've had a lot of time to
write on trains this week, so buckle up!

Tuesday
Today was literally filled with Miracles. I'm so grateful for God's hand in
my life, and I saw it demonstrated to me in a few big ways today. Yesterday
(pday) We headed up to Tottori to stay the night for DCM today. It's a
pretty messy apartment, really makes you grateful for your own situation
lol. Throughout the night I woke up like 10 times because I was
uncomfortable, and also had to kick a bunch of dust or crumbs off of my
futon. It was less than desirable, but when I got up in the morning, I felt
rejuvenated! First thing that God showed me today! Next, we headed out to
walk to the church for DCM. Alas, the curse of companions with poor sense
of direction strikes again. The church was supposed to be a 5 minute walk,
but we somehow walked almost 20 minutes past it =F0=9F=98=85 and everyone h=
ad to wait
us to start. I really should have just looked at a map before we left, but
it was OK in the end lol. DCM was pretty fun, but the trio of sister
missionaries in our district is definitely going through some conflicts
lol. Keep them in your prayers! Haha. Afterwards we went and got some Indo
curry, and I tried some lychee berries. Pretty interesting. We had to leave
in a hurry to catch our trains, poor Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 was dying i=
n the heat =F0=9F=98=82
While waiting at a station for our Next train, Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 h=
ad to go to the
bathroom, so I was sitting alone Waiting on a bench in the station. I hear
a voice say =E2=80=9Chello?=E2=80=9D This foreigner sits down by me and we =
introduce
ourselves to each other! His name was Berihun, and he's from Ethiopia! He's
been living in Japan for Like 3-4 years Studying to be a veterinarian
Researcher. Super cool. I was able to talk with him about religion, and he
told me he reads from the Bible and is Christian. I introduced the Book of
Mormon, and testified of how Jesus taught and loves his Children all over
the world, and how his teachings to the American people are written in the
Book of Mormon. He seemed very interested, and when I gave him an English
copy of the book, he took it very excitedly and said He's gonna read it! I
was able to exchange information with him, and he happens to live like a
block away from the church in Tottori! He wants to meet with the
missionaries and is also excited to practice Japanese with them. Huge
miracle!!!!!! =E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F=F0=9F=
=93=A2=F0=9F=9A=A8=F0=9F=9A=A8 I just wish bro lived in our area! =F0=9F=98=
=82 The Lord
is preparing people all over the world to receive the restored gospel, and
Berihun is a great example of this! I hope I can meet him again someday =F0=
=9F=98=81
OK one last miracle from Today. On the way back home riding many trains, I
realized that the key to my bike wasn't in my pocket like it usually is. If
I didn't have it things were going to be so rough when we got back home,
considering it's an hour and a half walk to the apartment. I realized this,
calmed down, and trusted that God would provide a way. I said a prayer, and
afterwards reached right into my backpack and pulled out my key. Super
grateful for God's help =F0=9F=99=8F I promise that we are loved and watche=
d over,
and that God shows this to us in a variety of ways.

Wednesday
Today we didn't really have any outside finding time, but we made some good
preparations and taught Kids Eikaiwa! Well, I'd like to say that =E2=80=9Cw=
e=E2=80=9D
taught it, but my companion ended up taking like a 30 minute phone call in
the muddle of it so I handled things by myself (OK so we didn't teach but
we assisted =F0=9F=98=81=F0=9F=98=82) I am at first super awkward teaching =
little kids stuff
but once I got into it and jumped around and clapped my hands it got better
lol. Be as a child and you can teach the children =F0=9F=94=A5

Thursday
=F0=9F=8C=9FElder Killian deep dive=F0=9F=8C=9F
This morning for part of my personal study I watched a video addressed to
newly called missionaries, inviting them to think about what kind of a
person they want to be when they return home. Now that I'm halfway through
my mission, I can't go back and change the first year, but this next year
is in my control; I want to make the most of it. Here's a few things I=E2=
=80=99m
going to try and implement for future me:

Financial Awareness
Prioritizing
Goal Setting
Daily Scripture Study
Humility
Understanding of Both Parties
Using Technology Efficiently
Gospel Art
Always Placing Others=E2=80=99 Needs Above My Wants

I have already learned so much from a mission, it's crazy to ponder. I feel
like I am a much more humble and understanding person than before my
mission, I'm so grateful for the experiences that have led me to the =E2=80=
=9CMe=E2=80=9D I
am today. However, if I feel that I've changed a lot from just 1 year of a
mission, I know I'll be surprised by what challenges and growth
opportunities I see in these next months. I would absolutely recommend
anyone reading this contemplating a mission to think about what they are
looking to improve about themselves. While the focus of a mission should be
outward, there are just so many things that you can learn about yourself
from a mission. The challenges and effort are absolutely worth it. I
encourage you to pray about a mission, and seek to know if it is right for
you.

A couple dreams

I had a pretty freaky dream this Tuesday =E2=80=A6 on the underside of my r=
ight
forearm I have an abnormally long strand of peach fuzz, about an inch or
two long. Even when I plucked it off once, I'm pretty sure it just grew
right back. (This is a real life explanation lol) Anyways, in this dream
instead of being a strand of hair, it was my nerves sticking out of my arm.
Like all throughout my dream my nerves in my arm kept getting like pushed
out, and whenever they brushed against anything it was like hitting your
funny bone. I could kind of slide them back into my arm if I was careful,
but through the dream they just kept sliding out =F0=9F=92=80 very weird an=
d
disturbing

I had another dream on Thursday night. I remember at one point in this
dream I was trying to explain my first dream to someone, which was really
weird lol. I think this dream mostly took place in my house. One highlight
was that my youngest brother, Kameron, was trying to convince us that we
needed to watch like 2=C2=BD hours of new Bluey episodes with him. There wa=
s
also some point in my dream with pokemon cards, and also a pretty big
robotic spider, which my mom was controlling. I think my mom might have
also been partially a robot or something lol. Interest dreams =F0=9F=98=82

Friday
I've come to a pretty interesting realization. This Week my head has been
seriously hurting quite a bit. I've taken medicine and have Been drinking
lots of water, but it doesn't seem to be affecting anything very much. I
think I have an idea as to what might be wrong though =F0=9F=91=80 I'm pret=
ty sure I
have a minor concussion =F0=9F=98=AE Looking back on things my head has bee=
n hurting
since that 70 year old guy smacked me in the side of the head, I lowkey
think it's from that =F0=9F=98=82 We are gonna try and call the medical coo=
rdinator
tomorrow but a concussion would match up with my symptoms I think. Besides
this interesting revelation, we were able to meet at the Okada family's
house and practice music! This time we walked up to the second floor, and
into a super cool room filled with all kinds of cool music stuff. We were
able to practice our songs for the concert together, it was super fun! I
even got to hook my guitar up to a big Amp =F0=9F=98=8E=F0=9F=98=8E=F0=9F=
=98=8E=F0=9F=98=8E=F0=9F=8E=B8=F0=9F=8E=B8=F0=9F=8E=B8=F0=9F=8E=B8=F0=9F=8E=
=B8=F0=9F=8E=B8=E2=9A=A1=EF=B8=8F=E2=9A=A1=EF=B8=8F=E2=9A=A1=EF=B8=8F=E2=9A=
=A1=EF=B8=8F=E2=9A=A1=EF=B8=8F
It was awesome. I held back from playing some hard rock stuff but It would
have sounded so cool =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=82

Saturday
Today was also a bit slow. My head was really hurting today, but we were
able to talk with the mission medical coordinator. His name is Elder Brown,
and he's a riot. He doesn't think I have a serious concussion since I'm not
throwing up and my vision isn't impaired, but he thinks it might be a minor
concussion. If things get any worse I'm supposed to go to a clinic. For now
I=E2=80=99m just gonna keep trying medicine and hanging in there. Today we =
actually
had a really cool experience giving a priesthood blessing for the sick and
afflicted to a non member. There's a lady named Tsukiyama san and she has a
broken leg. It makes it really hard for her to run her store, and Hattori=
=E4=BC=9A=E9=95=B7
suggested we visit her together. Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 had the awesome=
 idea to ask her
if we could give her a blessing. She actually agreed when asked by
Hattori=E4=BC=9A=E9=95=B7! We were able to go to her store, and we blessed =
her to be able
to heal quickly and according to her faith. It was a really neat
experience. I made an art letter for her and Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 mad=
e some Origami.
She was super grateful, and reassured by the blessing! aside from that,
there wasn't anything big that stood out from today besides getting some
ice cream from a drugstore =F0=9F=98=8E=F0=9F=86=92=EF=B8=8F

Sunday
Last night I dreamed that I was playing piano over at my grandma's house
and ended up startling her. She was happy to see me though! I was on a
video call with my mom and my aunt at the same time too. They wanted me to
show them grandma, so I panned around my phone to show them the room and
she had left so they couldn't see her, and I commented saying she was a
=E2=80=9Cpart-time=E2=80=9D grandma lol. I thought it was pretty funny. At =
some other point
in my dream I was viewing my mom's video call and she was fighting off a
bunch of feral raccoons in a backyard, it was pretty awesome lol. One other
odd quote from my dream too. There was some father in the dream (not my
father) and he was talking about his American kids saying that even though
they know only English, that when he whispers about then in Japanese they
can tell what he says like it was English. Something like that. I also
thought it was pretty funny in the dream =F0=9F=98=85=F0=9F=98=82

As for the real life side of things, this Sunday is pretty crazy already as
I'm writing things. We got up and used our morning mostly for getting ready
for zone conference, and then went to church, prepared to leave soon after.
Seems like the curse of =E2=80=9Ccompanions with no sense of direction=E2=
=80=9D is back
again this transfer =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=82. We need to travel all the way=
 to Yonago For our
Zone Conference, but we ended up being on the wrong platform and missed our
train, which only sets us back about 3 HOURS =F0=9F=92=80 lol. Waiting 3 ho=
urs in the
semi-heat at a station is no fun. I could probably get mad at my companion
and it would be valid, but it's already in the past, so no use making a big
deal about things =F0=9F=99=83 it is a long time to wait though, not mentio=
ning the
4+ hours of travel we have afterwards. It's about using this time as
efficiently as we can. We'll see how it goes =F0=9F=98=85=F0=9F=98=82

