Zone Conference (Monday)
Today was a pretty unique zone conference experience! It was kind of a
youth missionary training experience, and at the start we got assigned
individually to about 2-3 youth to be their companions for the day. I ended
up with Elder Kenshin, Elder Inoue, and Elder Matsumoto. (Not really Elders
haha) the 3 of them were really neat, but I only got a picture with Elder
Inoue at the end =F0=9F=98=AD We had a bunch of cool activities and Role Pl=
ay
lessons. It was interesting to think about how I would bear my testimony
and teach a lesson when I was 15 or so. It would be hard. Elder Matsumoto I
think was around 15 or 16 and it was his responsibility to do a lot of
sharing and teaching. He's a bit of a quiet guy but he hung in there and
gave it his best. I tried to encourage him, and at the end I shared in
front of everyone how he really brought the spirit to our lesson. I hope
that he grows up to be an awesome Missionary, he sure is now =F0=9F=98=81 I=
 had my
interview with Sano=E4=BC=9A=E9=95=B7 today which was fun. I asked him what=
 his favorite
dessert was and one of the foods he said was his wife's lemon scones. He
seemed surprised I haven't tried any, but I still haven't really served all
that close to Kobe yet =F0=9F=98=82 I asked Sano=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 about it=
 after the interview and
I'm pretty sure she wrote down my name, she's definitely gonna try and get
me some lemon scones =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=8D=8B Today I got two awesome packa=
ges from my family.
A new spikeball net!!! (I will not be entrusting this to any other Elders
lol) and a bunch of snacks and notes and fun things =F0=9F=99=83 I'm so gra=
teful to
have such a caring family. I'm also grateful for you! Yes, you, whichever
one of my friends or neighbors or family you are. I love you!

After zone conference we got geared up to travel back home. Seems like it's
gonna be a long ways, and pretty expensive. Hopefully we don't have any
missed train incidents this time around =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=82

Conclusion

This week has been pretty crazy. It's been super fun though. I've also had
a good chance to write my thoughts and evaluate things. I hope that we can
have more finding time this next week, but it's also been important
strengthening the members that live here as much as we can. I know that God
loves each of us, and that Jesus Christ loves us too. He is our Savior!
Isn't that a huge miracle?! One last miracle is that I have people like you
reading my email. I'm so blessed to have met so many amazing people in my
short 20 years I've been alive. Thank you for all that you mean to and have
done for me. Love you =F0=9F=92=9C!

Elder Killian

